#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:48
msgid "faq-prod-madeitaly"
msgstr "Are all the products 100% Made in Italy?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:49
msgid "faq-prod-madeitaly-body"
msgstr ""
"Absolutely yes, all our products are exclusively selected by us, from the "
"best Italian manufacturers. The clays used to make the tiles come from "
"Italian quarries which makes our products designed and manufactured on "
"Italian land. You will always find the Made In Italy brand on the incoming "
"boxes"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:52
msgid "faq-prod-multiface"
msgstr ""
"Will the tiles I receive be identical to those in the photo? What is meant "
"by the degree of shading?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:53
msgid "faq-prod-multiface-body"
msgstr ""
"Here a little explanation is needed: the best tiles reproduce natural "
"effects, and in nature it is difficult to find, for example, identical "
"wooden slabs or identical pebbles. A good tile will give the feeling of "
"being in front of the diversity of a natural product. This characteristic "
"bears the name of Degree of Shading. The characteristic of  this type of "
"products consists in having a differentiation of the faces of the individual "
"tiles, in order to obtain a visual result close to the naturalness of the "
"material from which the tile is inspired. The small sample you will receive "
"at home does not fully describe every inch of the tile itself. However, it "
"will help you to touch the surface effect and the color gradation live."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:57
msgid "faq-prod-handmade"
msgstr ""
"What is the difference between an industrial product and a handmade product?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:58
msgid "faq-prod-handmade-body"
msgstr ""
"Our industrial products are made with production phases in Italian factories "
"of the highest quality. The handmade products are instead made in compliance "
"with ancient manual techniques and are therefore always unique and "
"unrepeatable products."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:62
msgid "faq-prod-temperature"
msgstr "Do the tiles deteriorate in contact with heat or cold?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:63
msgid "faq-prod-temperature-body"
msgstr ""
"All industrial products in fine porcelain stoneware are anti-freeze, "
"therefore, resistant to frost. They also withstand very high temperatures "
"so, for example, a pan that has come out of the oven at home can be placed "
"on top without problems. The very high temperatures of the industrial "
"production process guarantee a product that remains intact and always the "
"same over time. Handmade products, on the other hand, are very different "
"from industrial products. Each product has different technical "
"characteristics, so we invite you to consult the technical data sheet of "
"each product you are interested in, otherwise contact us at <a href=\\"
"\"mailto:info@taleoftiles.com\\\">info@taleoftiles.com</a> "

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:67
msgid "faq-prod-maintenance"
msgstr ""
"What are the most easily washable products? Is it possible to wash them with "
"any detergent or is there a risk that they will be damaged or become dull?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:68
msgid "faq-prod-maintenance-body"
msgstr ""
"All commercial detergents can be used without fear of damaging or dulling "
"the tiles. The use of acid to clean them could, if not dried carefully, "
"damage the surface layer of the clay firing. Fine porcelain stoneware is "
"antibacterial, warm water is sufficient for thorough cleaning."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:72
msgid "faq-prod-decor"
msgstr "How does the product called \"decor\" work?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:73
msgid "faq-prod-decor-body"
msgstr ""
"In products that bear the wording \"decoration\", the manufacturer will "
"insert, in each box, different designs from those available. It is not "
"possible, neither for us nor for you, to choose a single face among those "
"available in the \"decoration\" version, nor to predict how many faces of "
"each image there will be inside the box. It will be a bit like opening a "
"pack of stickers."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:77
msgid "faq-prod-fughe"
msgstr ""
"Are glue joints always necessary? Can I lay the tiles next to each other "
"without the grout showing?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:78
msgid "faq-prod-fughe-body"
msgstr ""
"The joint is always necessary when laying tiles to compensate for the "
"natural expansion of the materials. Even when the product is rectified, that "
"is with perfectly straight edges, even if only by one millimeter, we always "
"recommend mounting with the joint. You can play a lot with the visibility of "
"the joint by carefully choosing the color of the grout to obtain a less "
"visible final effect."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:86
msgid "faq-sample-1"
msgstr "What's the Tale of Tiles Book?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:87
msgid "faq-sample-1-body"
msgstr ""
"Tale of Tiles Book is a customisable sample that will allow you to touch our "
"products firsthand and be able to appreciate every detail. Contains 4 "
"samples of tiles of your choice, which we give you so that you can carefully "
"evaluate your choice. You will receive a completely free Tale of Tiles Book "
"directly to your home. With Tale of Tiles Book you will be the one to write "
"the history of your home."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:91
msgid "faq-sample-2"
msgstr "How much does the Tale of Tiles Book cost?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:92
msgid "faq-sample-2-body"
msgstr ""
"Your first Tale of Tiles Book is shipped directly to your home for free. If "
"you want to receive other Tale of Tiles books at home, the next ones can be "
"purchased at a price of € 25 including transport, a cost that will be "
"deducted from the next order."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:96
msgid "faq-sample-3"
msgstr "Can I have more than one Tale of Tiles Book?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:97
msgid "faq-sample-3-body"
msgstr ""
"Your first Tale of Tiles Book is always free, however it is possible to "
"request more than one and the following ones can be purchased at a price of "
"25 € including shipping costs, which will be deducted from your possible "
"order."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:101
msgid "faq-sample-4"
msgstr "Can I have a sample of a handmade product?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:102
msgid "faq-sample-4-body"
msgstr ""
"The handmade product cannot be sampled in the Tale of Tiles Book, but it is "
"always possible to request it. We invite you to contact us by email at <a "
"href=\\\"mailto:info@taleoftiles.com\\\">info@taleoftiles.com</a>  with your "
"personal request."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:106
msgid "faq-sample-5"
msgstr "How soon will I receive my Tale of Tiles Book?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:107
msgid "faq-sample-5-body"
msgstr ""
"The Tale of Tiles Book is shipped directly to your home by express courier. "
"Upon delivery of the package, you will be notified of the shipment tracking. "
"Shipments are processed within 2 working days from the request for the Tale "
"of Tiles Book."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:115
msgid "faq-order-minmax"
msgstr "Are there any minimum or maximum limits on orders' quantities?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:116
msgid "faq-order-minmax-body"
msgstr ""
"For both industrial and artisanal products, the minimum quantity of m2 that "
"you can buy is indicated in the product sheet. These restrictions are due to "
"production limits. However, it is always possible to contact us at <a href=\\"
"\"mailto:orders@taleoftiles.com\\\">orders@taleoftiles.com</a>  to find a "
"solution even for small sizes. For orders over 200m2 contact us for the "
"“Large Quantity Discount”."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:119
msgid "faq-order-sfrido"
msgstr "What is meant by scrap?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:120
msgid "faq-order-sfrido-body"
msgstr ""
"The scrap is the calculation of the tile waste introduced by the laying "
"process. It is a calculation that involves several variables, such as the "
"size of the tiles compared to the shape of the room. The site automatically "
"calculates this additional quantity based on the order, and is the minimum "
"percentage recommended by manufacturers and installers. It is always "
"recommended to add it because during the laying phase waste is expected to "
"happens due to tile cuts. "

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:124
msgid "faq-order-payment"
msgstr "What payment methods do you accept?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:125
msgid "faq-order-payment-body"
msgstr "We accept Bank Transfer, PayPal and Credit Card"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:129
msgid "faq-order-return"
msgstr "How can I return the product if I change my mind?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:130
msgid "faq-order-return-body"
msgstr ""
"It is always possible to return the material that you will receive through "
"Tale of Tiles SrLs within 14 days of arrival at the place you indicated for "
"receiving the goods. If you want to return it, you can do so by filling out "
"the return request form available HERE. For logistical reasons, the material "
"to be transported back will have to be repackaged. For this reason, if you "
"change your mind and want to return the products you will have to take care "
"of resealing the pallet in the same way as when it was delivered to you. In "
"case of withdrawal you will be charged the cost of transport. Your payment "
"will be returned to you within 30 days of receiving the returned goods."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:136
msgid "faq-transport-cost"
msgstr "How much does it cost and what does the transport include?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:137
msgid "faq-transport-cost-body"
msgstr ""
"Receiving the tiles from Tale of Tiles to your home is free unless in "
"exceptional cases such as islands, limited traffic areas or areas with "
"difficult or remote access. If you think your delivery is one of these "
"cases, write to us at <a href=\\\"mailto:orders@taleoftiles.com\\"
"\">orders@taleoftiles.com</a> before placing your order to receive a "
"personalised shipping quote. The transport does not include porterage. Ours "
"is a standard transport with tail lift on the ground, in areas that can be "
"easily reached by means of transport."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:140
msgid "faq-transport-track"
msgstr "Where is my shipment located?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:142
msgid " faq-transport-track-body "
msgstr ""

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:146
msgid "faq-shipping-timeind"
msgstr "What are the delivery times for industrial products?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:147
msgid "faq-shipping-timeind-body"
msgstr ""
"For each product, you will find the necessary processing time on its page. "
"Before you complete the order, we will confirm the exact timing for "
"receiving your tiles. We guarantee delivery within the deadlines "
"communicated at the time of the order. If there are delays due to the "
"production of your tiles, you will have the opportunity to reconsider and "
"withdraw the purchase and the full amount paid will be returned to you "
"within 24 hours."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:150
msgid "faq-shipping-timehandm"
msgstr "What are the delivery times for handmade products?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:151
msgid "faq-shipping-timehandm-body"
msgstr ""
"Even for handmade products, as for industrial ones, in each product sheet "
"you will find delivery times, which will be confirmed at the time of "
"purchase. Times may vary because since these are hand-made products, the "
"processing may vary according to the required quantities."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:154
msgid "faq-shipping-broken"
msgstr ""
"What do I do if the material arrives damaged or if the package containing it "
"is not intact?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:155
msgid "faq-shipping-broken-body"
msgstr ""
"When you complete your order, the instructions to follow to follow the "
"shipment of your tiles will arrive by email. All materials sold on Tale of "
"Tiles have undamaged delivery guaranteed by the manufacturer to your door. "
"If the package should be damaged or opened or the material damaged, you can "
"choose whether to receive a refund or whether to receive the goods again."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:161
msgid "faq-company-1"
msgstr "Where is the company headquarters located?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:162
msgid "faq-company-1-body"
msgstr ""
"Tale of Tiles is an all-Italian company based in Forano (RI). We select for "
"you the materials produced in the Italian territory by companies with which "
"we have been collaborating for years and which guarantee us value for money, "
"reliability and continuous updates. Our young team is looking for the latest "
"trends in materials and decorations."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:165
msgid "faq-company-2"
msgstr "Do you produce the tiles?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:166
msgid "faq-company-2-body"
msgstr ""
"No, the tiles are not made by us. We are retailers with experience gained in "
"10 years of retail sale of Made in Italy floor and wall coverings. For this "
"reason we are able to select only the best of the Italian industrial and "
"handmade scene."

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:170
msgid "faq-company-3"
msgstr "Is it possible to visit you in person?"

#: taleoftiles/templates/support.html:171
msgid "faq-company-3-body"
msgstr ""
"For over 10 years we have owned a showroom with a physical store in Forano "
"(RI), in the countryside of central Italy, on the border between Umbria and "
"Lazio (easily accessible by train from Fiumicino airport)."

